<title>UK: Minerva Plc to acquire London property.</title>
<headline>Minerva Plc to acquire London property.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minerva Plc has exchanged contracts for the purchase of the head leasehold interest of St Botolph's House in central London for 28.7 million stg.</p>
<p>Minerva will pay current owners Avondale (City) Limited 6.7 million stg cash and take on the existing 22 million stg mortgage on the property.</p>
<p>St Botolph's House is an office and retail site, the main tenant being British Telecommunications Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
